| def round(self, decimals: int = 0, *args, **kwargs) -> Series:\n2464 |         \"\"\"\n2465 |         Round each value in a Series to the given number of decimals.\n2466 | \n2467 |         Parameters\n2468 |         ----------\n2469 |         decimals : int, default 0\n2470 |             Number of decimal places to round to. If decimals is negative,\n2471 |             it specifies the number of positions to the left of the decimal point.\n2472 |         *args, **kwargs\n2473 |             Additional arguments and keywords have no effect but might be\n2474 |             accepted for compatibility with NumPy.\n2475 | \n2476 |         Returns\n2477 |         -------\n2478 |         Series\n2479 |             Rounded values of the Series.\n2480 | \n2481 |         See Also\n2482 |         --------\n2483 |         numpy.around : Round values of an np.array.\n2484 |         DataFrame.round : Round values of a DataFrame.\n2485 | \n2486 |         Notes\n2487 |         -----\n2488 |         For values exactly halfway between rounded decimal values, pandas rounds\n2489 |         to the nearest even value (e.g. -0.5 and 0.5 round to 0.0, 1.5 and 2.5\n2490 |         round to 2.0, etc.).\n2491 | \n2492 |         Examples\n2493 |         --------\n2494 |         >>> s = pd.Series([-0.5, 0.1, 2.5, 1.3, 2.7])\n2495 |         >>> s.round()\n2496 |         0   -0.0\n2497 |         1    0.0\n2498 |         2    2.0\n2499 |         3    1.0\n2500 |         4    3.0\n2501 |         dtype: float64\n2502 |         \"\"\"\n2503 |         nv.validate_round(args, kwargs)\n2504 |         new_mgr = self._mgr.round(decimals=decimals)\n2505 |         return self._constructor_from_mgr(new_mgr, axes=new_mgr.axes).__finalize__(\n2506 |             self, method=\"round\"\n2507 |         )\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"round\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/frame.py:DataFrame.round`.\nFound function `pandas/core/internals/blocks.py:Block.round`.\nFound function `pandas/cor